   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capabilities and opportunities of businesses to set up and expand higher value-added production increased</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">c. Estimate of regulatory quality increased to -0.50 in 2017 (subprogram 2) and -0.25 in 2019 
(2014 baseline: -1.00; 2015 baseline: -1.01) 
Data Source: c. World Bank&apos;s Worldwide Governance Indicators (www.govindicators.org) 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="-1.01" year="2015"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2017-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2017-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="-0.5"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">b. Proportion of firms in Tajikistan that reports having an internationally recognized quality certification increased to at least 22% by 2017 (subprogram 2) and 25% by 2019 
(2013 baseline: 17%; 2015 baseline: 14%) 
Data Source: b. World Economic Forum&apos;s Global Competitiveness Report 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="14" year="2015"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2017-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2017-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="22"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 4</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">d. Share of women as a percentage of entrepreneurs increased to 25.0% in 2017 (subprogram 2) and 30.0% in 2016-2019
(2010-2014 baseline: average of 19.9%) 
Data Source: d. Tajikistan National Statistics Committee, gender analysis 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="20" year="2014"></baseline>
